                <pb facs="0833" n="735" sameAs="frus:frus1930v02/pg735"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">836.48 1930 Hurricane/41: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Minister in the
                        Dominican Republic</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Curtis</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-09-10">September 10, 1930</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>49. Major Watson proceeding on destroyer <hi rendition="#italic">Gilmer</hi>,
                    which left Hampton Roads this morning. He will probably arrive at Santo Domingo
                    September 12. He is being designated as Naval Attaché with a view to his
                    assignment as Food Administrator, as requested by the Dominican Republic.
                    Further formal instructions follow.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Cotton</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
